                <pb facs="0954" n="826" xml:id="pg826"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79620 Boeing Airplane Co./38: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-01-08T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 8,
                                1929—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Department’s 38, September 26, 3 p.m. Captain O’Neil states that contract was
                    signed by the Director of Posts with Tri-Motors Airways December 22, subject to
                    approval by other officials. Please report present status of the matter and
                    possibilities of final ratification of the contract in the near future. Lend all
                    appropriate assistance to O’Neil’s representative and report by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
